## Relics
Now you would think this one is easy right, well it would be if there wasn't a thing called 'Relic Coupons' or
'Rewarding Elites'. The main problem with these is the race conditions and the chests. The problem with chests is that
due to race conditions and timings: one person may see 1 relic in the chest while another may see 0, 1 or 2 relics in the chest
and this breaks the game. So you need to manually freeze the progress when you reach the chest: the host is authoritative here and says
ok here: P1 has X counter in their coupons, P2 has Y counter in their coupons etc hence why a 
non-host player has big lag when opening the chest.
They're asking the host for what they did. There's also a feature whereby players can't open the reward menu until everyone else opened
the chest. Now it's been like 1-2 weeks since I implemented it: but I think it was due to choice 23: akabeko choice 24: anchor but the other
players saw choice 23: anchor choice 24: abakeko. So the effects were the same but the ordering was broken so state divergence.
Simple fix was to just disable opening the menu in chests period, 2nd harder fix was to allow opening the menu 
after everyone opened the menu. But yes a lot of syncing is required to handle the 'rewarding' elites.
Who knows if it was worth it. 
There's a few alternate options: kill off the rewarding elites and the coupons and put everything in the ap menu.
Like a suggestion was to just pre-generate the relics (not all 10 of them of course) and disable the button if you didn't get enough
natural relics. Not a bad suggestion: probably would still need some syncing at the chest (confirm this but probably less syncing)
however backshot, you can't steal your friends relics at the chest which is infinitely less funny.
Also yeah had to do some fixes when there are less relics than there are players.
Oh i forgot to mention but relics need our own rng handling: believe me i've tried many other methods but there's always some funky
weird race condition or tutorial relics that just break everything because one player said they don't allow this relic but the other person
didn't know and the AP menu somehow bypassed that check when generating.
Simplest fix was our own rng: now i don't exactly remember why the other methods didn't work
but they didn't work. So yeah extra reason why relics didn't work and why they were bad.

