## Card Rewards
If you thought Relics weer tough: then I don't blame you.
Let's start simple with Card Reward Checks: 
Well for starters you NEED to know your other player's AP settings. And you need a counter for them specifically
You need to know whether or not your peers have a Card Reward or a check and this matters because one advances rng and the other doesn't.
Believe me i'd know. state divergences will pop up out of nowhere.
If we ever reworked say card rewards from events, prayer wheel, card rewards from relics to give checks then this stuff goes from 
baby playground sleeping to like triple threat world war level things.

Well Card Reward Checks weren't so bad, what could go wrong...
EVERYTHING. Well for one you can't just copy what you did with potions or gold or relics in the AP menu:
because card rewards have a little interesting thing called relics affecting them. You can't just say hey I picked this card, give that to
me. Nope, because that bypasses the relic hooks n stuff (maybe there's a way to do so now that i've refactored enough).
Did I also mention that our card rewards also break the laws of the base game a lot: skipping doesn't actually skip, the card rewards
are saved and persisted: they aren't discarded. We allow gaining more than one card at one time and claimed at the same time as other 
relics. The base game really doesn't like this: in fact it generates your card rewards before you even view them. So what people think
of as oh relic X should just work: nope it requires more handling on our part.
I guess most of the gripe with card rewards isn't the multiplayer aspect but also partly the base game handling of it
In that sense relics might be complicated in multiplayer handling.

Anyway, the current method tries to follow the base game a lot:
It uses our own rng thing for multiplayer handling. Oh wait now im remembering. We had a lot of hassle 
because of relics that interact with card rewards: things like pael's wing which advances megacrit RNG (LIKE WHY):
and it advances it in such a way that it breaks everything. I don't exactly remember why it wasn't a small fix but our 
rewards are different enough that it just wasn't. Oh it was also because just rolling the pity roll also advances rng.
So i had to do a huge compromise and re-implement parts of the card reward system and I intentionally left parts out.
This was really annoying to do. 
But it doesn't stop there: there's the egg relics, silken tress, silver crucible and glitter which are also really painful..
In this case silken tress and silver crucible are the bigger nightmares.
